    "lawCode": "Add §6438-b, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1213A\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to providing access to\nmedication abortion prescription drugs at the state university of New\nYork and the city university of New York\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would require SUNY and CUNY to ensure access to medication\nabortion to all enrolled students.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the education law by adding a new section 6438-b to\nrequire every SUNY and CUNY campus to provide access to medication\nabortion to all enrolled students.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFor decades, medication abortion has provided a safe, non-invasive, and\neffective way to end a pregnancy. According to Planned Parenthood, the\nmedication has a less than 1% rate of complication and a near 100% rate\nof effectively terminating pregnancy, making it one of the safest and\nmost effective medications.\n\nMedication abortion is different than the \"morning after pill,\"which is\ntypically already available at public university student health centers.\nWhile the morning after pill is intended to prevent pregnancy from\noccurring, medication abortion is intended to prevent an existing preg-\nnancy from progressing. This bill would ensure that our public colleges\nprovide students with access to these medication abortion prescription\ndrugs.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: A.3322-A (Epstein) - Referred to Higher Education\n\n2019-2020:  A.8743 (Epstein) - Referred to Higher Education\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect August 1, 2023.\n",
